\description{
\code{RSKeyValuePair} defines an abstract base class for representing a key-value pair structure
used in robjc's dictionary-like containers. This class provides the minimal core logic for
key-value encapsulation, including accessors and equality/hash operations based solely on the key.

Subclasses of \code{RSKeyValuePair} are responsible for enforcing type or protocol constraints.
For example:
\itemize{
\item \code{RSClassReference} requires the key to conform to the \code{RSEncoding} protocol.
}

This class itself does not perform any protocol checks or validation; it simply stores and compares keys and values.
}
